| **Medium** | EPW parser extracts absolute extremes (not ASHRAE 99.6%/0.4% design conditions) and mixes non-dry-bulb parameters via a parameter-agnostic toggle heuristic. The proper ASHRAE design values are present in the TMY3 header's `Heating`/`Cooling` sections but are ignored. |
| **Low** | No distance guard on ASHRAE 152 nearest-station haversine lookup. |
| **Low** | Hardcoded defaults (-10°C/35°C) misleadingly labeled "conservative" — though unreachable in practice (only fires for (0,0) sentinel). |
| **Low** | Site vs. weather coordinates: no distance warning when they differ significantly. |
| **Informational** | Heating/cooling design temps are correctly separated — no cross-contamination. |

The overall fallback chain is **safe but imprecise**: all three steps over-size rather than under-size equipment. The main actionable issue is the EPW parser bypassing explicit ASHRAE design condition values already present in the TMY3 header in favor of a blurrier "Extremes" heuristic.
